You now are in the API Reference section where you can find detailed information about the Custom API: the Front-end API class, all available methods, types, attributes and decorators detailed descriptions can be found starting from this page. This page is about the CustomAPI class, which exposes high-level methods for easy access to the API.<h3>Example</h3><pre><code>from pytgcalls import CustomApi

api = CustomApi()

@api.on_update_custom_api()
async def custom_api_request(request: dict):
    print(request)
    return {
        &#39;response&#39;: &#39;FOXES&#39;,
    }
api.start()</code></pre>

example.code:
from pytgcalls import CustomApi

api = CustomApi()

@api.on_update_custom_api()
async def custom_api_request(request: dict):
    print(request)
    return {
        'response': 'FOXES',
    }
api.start()

